we've just been hearing from nicolas  sturgeon saying that this isn't a  grown-up conversation should we have one  about what is happening with public  health in  this part of the northwest in scotland  and why we've got this position of a  almost of accusations flying across the  border know  a conversation would be nice if the  scottish government had picked up the  phone because it's they've  changed the policy and you know that has  impacted on  on people here so i think nicholas  students say i should pick up the phone  well i'm  more than happy to but shouldn't they  have picked up the phone before they  before they they did this i i want to  hear from her how this  can be fair so today for instance bolton  has a significantly lower case rate than  dundee  bolton is under this travel ban dundee  is not  so i think we need an explanation from  the scottish government what are the  criteria that are being used here to  introduce these  decisions you know and is there going to  be any support  for individuals affected i've had emails  over the weekend  from uh residents of greater monster who  are thousands of pounds out of pocket as  a result of these changes  the scottish government has said this is  a sensible and proactive decision  to ensure that those variants are  suppressed as much as possible  and they can see the data here in north  the northwest of england  and those particular hotspots are the  ones that they've identified  you just don't accept it but we'll make  it consistent then  you know if there's a clear consistent  policy it should apply equally to any  cities in this position so  if bolton is under a travel ban with  cases under  300 then certainly dundee should be in  one with cases over  300 i'm not against taking action to  protect people's  health i just want to be assured that  it's fair  i'm being consistently applied across  across all areas and i have to say make  sure it's proportionate  so a couple you've emailed me have both  double jabbed  and they were going to book you know a  holiday in the scottish countryside  is that proportionate to say that they  can't they can't go  i personally don't think it is i don't  think the policy has been properly  thought through and i think the  government in scotland owes it to people  here to tell us  what are the criteria you know why a ban  still in place when cases are lower in  bolton  and how long will the ban be in place  here on city centre manchester and  salford you know  the first minister takes the stage on on  friday with no warning to anybody and  announces that  you know the uk's second city is going  under a travel ban  well that has an impact you know people  hear that statement being made it has an  impact  beyond just scottish visitors coming  people around the world will think  what's happening in manchester it's it's  it's very discourteous  not to me to the people of greater  manchester for this to be done  in this way in quite a high-handed way  without any explanation or or any  as i said any compensation for the loss  that people are suffering  i think i know the answer to this  question but is this about your  posturing and political ambition  i i just think she's insulting people  here who are emailing me  because i'm speaking up for them you  know to kind of make it all as though  that you know  it's all about politics you know and  none of this is real well i'll send  the first minister the the emails that  i've had and you know then maybe she  will see that it's  that it's real and you know the smp are  always the first aren't they  always the first to say oh the  westminster government has just done  something to us it didn't speak to us  and it's not fair  well we're a devolved administration too  here in greater manchester  i was elected by an electorate that  covers 2.8 million  people we have a measure of devolution  from from westminster  you know you would expect there to be  an understanding of that from the  scottish government but it just feels to  me  and particularly with this response it's  all about politics they're treating the  north of england with the same contempt  that the uk government  treats the north of england i speak out  about that when it's the the uk  government doing it but  i'm not going to not speak out about it  when it's the scottish government that  does the same  i mentioned to our viewers that you were  launching an environmental initiative  today a clean air zone for greater  manchester just  outline the bullet points of what you're  trying to achieve well from  may 30th next year all 10 boroughs of  greater manchester will become part of  the  the country's largest clean air zone but  unlike the scheme in birmingham  it will not include private cars  and it is not a congestion charge  because once people have got a clean  vehicle  there is there is no there is no charge  what we've done though is we've worked  with the government and thank you to  them for helping us with more financial  support  we can now offer people more time to  change more money  to change their their vehicle and we  think we can do this without a single  job or business  being lost but you know coming out of  the pandemic we've got to get more  serious about health  we can't tolerate things that we  tolerated before such as road pollution  that is harmful to the health  of the residents of greater manchester  it is time now to embrace  change but as we bring in a clean air  zone we're going to use it as a catalyst  to change public transport in greater  manchester putting our buses under  public control  integrating them with trams a new bike  hire scheme with e-bikes coming in today  all of it integrated  into one system called the b network  it's an exciting vision for our city  region

